idence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... His poems appear in Eastlit, Asian American Literary Review, TAYO Literary Magazine, and Cha: An Asian Literary Journal. He holds an MFA from Emerson College and works at a public library.\\n\\nERIC ROY's poems have appeared or are forthcoming from Bennington Review, Green Mountains Review, Salamander, Salt ... \",\"title\":\"https://lilypoetryreview.blog/issue-six-contributors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... Henry James said \\\"Kipling strikes me personally as the most complete man of genius, as distinct from fine intelligence, that I have ever known.\\\" In 1907, he was awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature, as the first English-language writer to receive the prize, and at 41, its ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudyard_Kipling\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... Robert Lowell and Robert Pinsky.[241] During John Silber's tenure as president, he recruited two Nobel Prize–winning literary figures to the university's faculty: Elie Wiesel, winner of the 1986 Nobel Peace Prize, and Saul Bellow, winner of the 1976 Nobel Prize in Literature.[241] Another ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_University\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sharon Olds - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2005-01-28\\n---\\nname: Sharon Olds\\nimage_upright: 0.9\\nbirth_date: 19 November 1942\\nbirth_place: San Francisco, California, U.S.\\neducation: Stanford University (BA)Columbia University (MA, PhD)\\noccupation: Poet\\nawards: Pulitzer Prize in Poetry, T. S. Eliot Prize, National Book Critics ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharon_Olds\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"ce1874a739c61dc229a166acda69d85d56a81a62443c83544d511f983b892feb\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"6cebe5c51cfd49d417852e550a1d1baee7226e77f123882de0b3b5450c9915e0\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize site:wikipedia.org\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... He was born in 1968 in Hyderabad, Pakistan, and now divides his time between Toronto and Karachi. His acclaimed new novel, Between Clay and Dust, was shortlisted for The Man Asian Literary Prize 2012 and longlisted for the 2013 DSC Prize for South Asian Literature. Farooqi's second ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/20-writers-from-around-the-world-on-the-olympics/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian writer, either written in English or translated into English, and published in the previous calendar year.\\n\\nFor many years, as part of The Times Literature ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":